erican Oil Rd, industry 327420); National Gypsum filed a WARN notice for its wallboard division there on 21 November 2008, reported at the time as the plant's…"},{"id":"2231f3fa-b854-4d1a-935d-e4384ec24699","from":"Northrop Grumman","name":"NEW NGC INC (DBA NATIONAL GYPSUM CO)","to":"National Gypsum","why":"National Gypsum's plant at 1502 W North Carrier Pkwy (the EPA's record: industry 327420, gypsum products, active)."},{"id":"446a908c-0b04-43c4-8297-e044d56e4bfa","from":"Northrop Grumman","name":"NEW NGC INC","to":"National Gypsum","why":"National Gypsum's plant at 832 County Rd 311 (the EPA's record: industry 327420, active). We already list this plant under National Gypsum as 'National Gypsum Rotan' (970199e4-8f22-4377-98ac-303217c958e3), written from sources, 380 m away: the two rows are one plant."},{"id":"b4f2600d-9a04-461e-a30f-1c91e4a86b15","from":"Northrop Grumman","name":"ALLIED-SIGNAL PRECISION PRODS, PLANT 2","to":"Alliedsignal","why":"AlliedSignal's, by its own name: one of the Norwood precision products plants AlliedSignal bought from Northrop Grumman in 1995 (AlliedSignal later became Honeywell, which I did not read on a page). There is a company row 'Allied-signal'. I found no current record of the plant and do not know that…"},{"id":"fc471cea-a313-4244-b91e-f711ee7062f3","from":"Raytheon","name":"RAYTHEON AIRCRAFT CO(WAS BEECH AIRCRAFT)","to":"Raytheon Aircraft","why":"Beech Aircraft's Boulder works, as the row's own name says ('RAYTHEON AIRCRAFT CO(WAS BEECH AIRCRAFT)'). Raytheon Aircraft was sold on 2007-03-26 to Hawker Beechcraft; it has not been Raytheon's since. I could not check whether the plant still works or under whom."},{"id":"f58f8e40-9e0f-4415-b818-493fa40d3cc9","from":"Raytheon","name":"RAYTHEON AIRCRAFT CO","to":"Raytheon Aircraft","why":"A Raytheon Aircraft (Beechcraft) site at 16121 East 13th Street, Andover, KS. Raytheon Aircraft was sold on 2007-03-26 to Hawker Beechcraft. I could not check whether it still works or under whom."},{"id":"ec918c11-1ef5-4716-8d8d-fa46035f8c0f","from":"Raytheon","name":"AMANA DELAWARE OPS","to":"Amana","why":"An Amana appliance plant. Raytheon sold Amana to Goodman Holding in 1997; the plant's toxics reports run 1987 to 1996, all under Raytheon. I could not check whether it works today or under whom."},{"id":"fe8bb3b1-4844-4a75-affa-e636d5e707b4","from":"Raytheon","name":"CALORIC CORP RAYTHEON COMPANY","to":"Caloric","why":"Caloric Corp, which the toxics inventory lists under Raytheon Co (a maker of home appliances as far as I know; no source I read says what it made). Its reports run 1987 to 1991 and stop: closed as far as the record shows, though the inventory does not mark it closed and I found no account of the…"},{"id":"18619965-7a17-48a7-aadb-39eacf5763bf","from":"Raytheon","name":"RESY-W MAEHR RD/TSTC AMF","mergeInto":"775bf94f-3fa6-4ed0-b1bd-6cee079308b5","intoName":"L3Harris Waco","why":"L3Harris's aircraft modification plant at Waco (7500 Maehr Rd, at the TSTC airfield): L3Harris files it with OSHA as 'L3Harris AS IAS Waco', aircraft manufacturing (336411), 1,400 people in 2024 and in 2025. It was Raytheon's until L-3 bought Raytheon's Aircraft Integration Systems in 2002. We…"},{"id":"6c3c8a9a-d311-4cf6-94e2-0a58688d1498","from":"Raytheon","name":"MACHLETT LABORATORIES INC C/O TUBE HOLDING CO","to":"Machlett Laboratories","why":"Machlett Laboratories, a tube maker by its row's own name ('C/O TUBE HOLDING CO'), which the toxics inventory lists under Raytheon Co at 1063 Hope St, Stamford; its reports run 1987 to 1989 and stop. Closed as far as the record shows; I found no account of what became of it."},{"id":"df2a4885-f1a4-433a-a858-9346362d8fe2","from":"Texas Instruments","name":"TEXAS INSTRUMENTS INC","mergeInto":"820ec88a-4f04-4ddc-b011-f4aa804c9cf3","intoName":"RAYTHEON TI SYSTEMS INCORPORATED","why":"A plant of TI's defense business (the EPA's record calls it Lewisville Defense Systems & Electronics), which TI sold in 1997; the Texas regulator's name for the site is now \"Raytheon Lewisville former Raytheon TI Systems\", and the Toxics Release Inventory holds TI's reports from it for 1987 to…"}]}$nt_data$::jsonb);
